# Code owners for digi-roll.
#
# A code owner is auto-requested for review on any PR touching these paths. It
# is only *enforced* if the ruleset on `main` has "Require review from Code
# Owners" turned on — see docs/adding-a-device.md and CLAUDE.md for why these
# particular files are the ones that matter.
#
# Owners must have write access to the repo, so this list stays as the repo
# owner until a second maintainer has been mapping boxes for a while.

# Default: everything gets a look.
*                               @zooloo303

# --- The hardware-verified encode/decode internals -------------------------
# Mapped byte-by-byte against real hardware; every byte layout in docs/ is
# derived from them. Compose them, don't edit them.
/js/elektron/sevenbit.js        @zooloo303
/js/elektron/protocol.js        @zooloo303
/js/elektron/pattern-core.js    @zooloo303
/js/elektron/dt2/pattern.js     @zooloo303
/js/elektron/dn2/pattern.js     @zooloo303

# --- The write path --------------------------------------------------------
# safe-write.js implements the five safety rules as one function so a caller
# can't skip one. Every write goes through it; nothing adds a sixth path.
/js/elektron/safe-write.js      @zooloo303
/js/elektron/backup-stash.js    @zooloo303

# --- The diff lab's read-only guard ---------------------------------------
# fetchDump and probeDumpRequests refuse any opcode outside 0x60-0x6e, because
# an 0x5n is what stores a payload on a box. The pitch to strangers is "this
# page cannot touch your patterns" and it has to stay literally true.
/js/elektron/device.js          @zooloo303
/js/labs/                       @zooloo303

# --- Ground truth ----------------------------------------------------------
# Hardware captures the test suite pins itself to, and the byte-level docs
# derived from them. Changing either invalidates a hardware verification.
/dumps/                         @zooloo303
/docs/elektron-sysex-protocol.md @zooloo303
/docs/dt2-pattern-format.md     @zooloo303
/docs/dn2-pattern-format.md     @zooloo303

# --- The rules themselves --------------------------------------------------
/CLAUDE.md                      @zooloo303
/.github/                       @zooloo303
